  "mechanisms": {
    "mouse": "xxxTrackMouse owns selection/modifiers, capture transitions and drag policy. xxxLBButtonUp kills scroll timer and clears fMouseDown/fCaptured before optional ReleaseCapture and notifications. Preserve this ordering, including recursive synthesized button-up on double click.",
    "keyboard": "Original keyboard navigation, range selection and type search stay C; original Compare uses native CompareStringW. Owner-draw WM_COMPAREITEM, WM_CHARTOITEM and WM_DRAWITEM retain their original data and notification rules.",
    "caretTimer": "Non-NULL timer callback is xxxLBoxCaretBlinker. F wow_control_set_timer maps it to list_caret_timer -> shared edit_entry -> list_caret_entry -> original callback. list_caret_entry validates retained WND/fnid before accessing LBIV; timer callback cannot be replaced with a raw SetTimer cast without considering current task/borrow entry. NULL timer callbacks share native SetTimer.",
    "drawing": "LBPrintCallback and original ClientDrawState remain C. F wow_control_draw_state supplies per-call scratch DC/bitmap ownership, nested TLS restoration and finally cleanup using current screen metrics; B system brushes are already separate. S13 must handle invocation lifetime, S14 original drawing-state composition; no new drawing engine.",
    "hitTest": "F wow_default_find_nc_hit reads original PWND handle, retains it in borrow scope, invokes native DefWindowProcW WM_NCHITTEST, and publishes return through shared native-call scope. Do not replace it with SendMessage to the same window.",
